: {"vendor": "Granite Facilities"}, "name": "list_invoices", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I paid Granite Facilities' approved invoice once, by wire, from the operating account.\n\n**Payment:**\n- **Payment ID:** PAY0001\n- **Invoice:** INV-34060 (due 2026-11-04), now marked **paid**\n- **Amount:** $7,058.54, the full invoice amount\n- **Method:** wire to Granite Facilities (vendor V-395, bank details verified)\n- **Status:** sent\n\n**What happened along the way:** My first wire request timed out. I checked the payment list twice and saw no payment and an unpaid invoice, so I tried the wire once more. The system rejected that second try because the invoice was \"already paid\": the first wire had gone through, it just showed up late. There is exactly one payment (PAY0001), with no duplicate and nothing to reverse. I didn't need to use ACH.\n\n**Notes:**\n- This is under the $10,000 limit, so it didn't need controller approval.\n- Granite Facilities has another invoice, INV-24483 for $6,826.80. It's still a draft waiting for approval, so I didn't pay it.", "type": "text"}]}]}